Experimental Android Vulkan support (feat/android-vulkan-experimental, #364).

1. Small-tile matmul warp layout. The small tiles are BM = BN = WN = 32, and
   their BLOCK_SIZE / WARP warps must tile BM / WM rows, so WM = 32 * WARP /
   BLOCK_SIZE. Upstream hard-codes WM = 32 for every subgroup size but 8, so
   with 16-wide subgroups (Mali Valhall and later, old Bifrost at 4, Intel
   MUL_MAT_ID tiles) the second warp lands on columns 32..63, outside its tile:
   every f32/f16 matmul with m <= 32, n >= 64 is wrong. No change for
   subgroup 8/32/64/128 (NVIDIA, AMD, Adreno, Apple).
   Found and verified on a Mali-G710 while testing codec.cpp.

2. Reject devices whose driver reports < Vulkan 1.2. The instance check only
   sees the loader version; Android loaders say 1.3 over 1.1 drivers, and
   device init then uses 1.2 feature structs. Also zero-initialise the feature
   query structs.

